#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Pengaturan {#setup}"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Contoh simulator skala kecil {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik ke masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-"
"inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We generate 20 random circuits with depth 4, where the number of qubits "
"ranges from six to 25. These circuits will serve as our test cases for "
"comparing transpilation strategies.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita membuat 20 Circuit acak dengan kedalaman 4, di mana jumlah qubit "
"berkisar dari enam hingga 25. Circuit-Circuit ini akan menjadi kasus uji "
"untuk membandingkan strategi transpilasi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
"introduction/extracted-outputs/sim-step1-code-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output dari sel kode sebelumnya](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
"introduction/extracted-outputs/sim-step1-code-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-"
"problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 2: Optimalkan masalah untuk eksekusi hardware kuantum "
"{#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We build the default (SABRE) pass manager for the chosen backend. Both "
"transpilation strategies target the backend's full coupling map. Local "
"simulation later stays tractable because the simulation step uses "
"`remap_to_contiguous` to relabel each transpiled circuit onto only its "
"active qubits, so Aer simulates just those qubits instead of the entire "
"device.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita membuat pass manager default (SABRE) untuk Backend yang dipilih. Kedua "
"strategi transpilasi menargetkan coupling map penuh Backend. Simulasi lokal "
"tetap dapat dikelola karena langkah simulasi menggunakan "
"`remap_to_contiguous` untuk menomori ulang setiap Circuit yang telah "
"ditranspilasi hanya pada qubit aktifnya, sehingga Aer hanya mensimulasikan "
"qubit-qubit tersebut dan bukan seluruh perangkat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The summary table shows the mean and standard deviation of each metric "
"across all 20 circuits, along with the average percentage improvement of the"
" AI-powered transpiler over the default. Positive values indicate the AI-"
"powered transpiler produced better results; negative values indicate the "
"default was better.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tabel ringkasan menunjukkan rata-rata dan standar deviasi setiap metrik di "
"seluruh 20 Circuit, beserta rata-rata persentase peningkatan Transpiler "
"bertenaga AI dibandingkan default. Nilai positif menunjukkan Transpiler "
"bertenaga AI menghasilkan hasil yang lebih baik; nilai negatif menunjukkan "
"transpiler default lebih unggul.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this small-scale example, the AI-powered transpiler achieves roughly 16%"
" lower two-qubit depth on average, but at the cost of roughly 9% higher gate"
" count. This highlights a key trade-off when choosing between the two "
"strategies: the AI-powered transpiler prioritizes depth reduction (fewer "
"sequential layers of two-qubit gates), while the default transpiler (SABRE) "
"prioritizes minimizing total gate count (fewer SWAP insertions). Depending "
"on your application, one metric may matter more than the other.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk contoh skala kecil ini, Transpiler bertenaga AI mencapai sekitar 16% "
"two-qubit depth yang lebih rendah rata-rata, namun dengan biaya sekitar 9% "
"jumlah Gate yang lebih tinggi. Ini menyoroti trade-off utama saat memilih "
"antara dua strategi: Transpiler bertenaga AI memprioritaskan pengurangan "
"kedalaman (lebih sedikit lapisan sekuensial Gate dua-Qubit), sedangkan "
"transpiler default (SABRE) memprioritaskan meminimalkan total jumlah Gate "
"(lebih sedikit penyisipan SWAP). Bergantung pada aplikasimu, satu metrik "
"mungkin lebih penting dari yang lain.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
"introduction/extracted-outputs/sim-step2-plot-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output dari sel kode sebelumnya](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
"introduction/extracted-outputs/sim-step2-plot-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
"introduction/extracted-outputs/sim-step2-plot-1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output dari sel kode sebelumnya](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
"introduction/extracted-outputs/sim-step2-plot-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Two-qubit depth:** The AI-powered transpiler generally produces circuits "
"with lower two-qubit depth. Depth is one of the primary metrics the AI "
"routing model is trained to optimize, and the improvement is visible across "
"most circuit sizes, though SABRE does match or beat it on individual "
"circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Two-qubit depth:** Transpiler bertenaga AI umumnya menghasilkan Circuit "
"dengan two-qubit depth yang lebih rendah. Depth adalah salah satu metrik "
"utama yang dilatih model routing AI untuk dioptimalkan, dan peningkatannya "
"terlihat di sebagian besar ukuran Circuit, meski SABRE terkadang menyamainya"
" atau mengunggulinya pada Circuit individual.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Gate count:** The results are closely matched at this scale, with SABRE "
"holding a slight edge overall. SABRE's routing heuristic is designed to "
"minimize the number of inserted SWAP gates, which directly reduces gate "
"count. At small circuit sizes, the difference is modest.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Jumlah Gate:** Hasilnya hampir sebanding pada skala ini, dengan SABRE "
"memiliki sedikit keunggulan secara keseluruhan. Heuristik routing SABRE "
"dirancang untuk meminimalkan jumlah Gate SWAP yang disisipkan, yang secara "
"langsung mengurangi jumlah Gate. Pada ukuran Circuit kecil, perbedaannya "
"tidak terlalu besar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Transpilation time:** SABRE's runtime is nearly constant regardless of "
"qubit count, so circuit size has little effect on its transpilation time at "
"this scale. SABRE's core routing logic is highly optimized (largely "
"implemented in Rust). The AI-powered transpiler takes noticeably longer and "
"scales with circuit size, though the absolute times remain reasonable for "
"interactive use.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Waktu transpilasi:** Waktu proses SABRE hampir konstan terlepas dari "
"jumlah qubit, sehingga ukuran Circuit sedikit berpengaruh pada waktu "
"transpilasi di skala ini. Logika routing inti SABRE sangat dioptimalkan "
"(sebagian besar diimplementasikan dalam Rust). Transpiler bertenaga AI "
"memerlukan waktu yang lebih lama dan skalanya bertumbuh seiring ukuran "
"Circuit, meski waktu absolutnya tetap wajar untuk penggunaan interaktif.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-"
"primitives}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 3: Eksekusi menggunakan Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-"
"qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To evaluate the impact of transpilation on circuit fidelity, build mirror "
"circuits from the 10-qubit case and run them on the Aer simulator with a "
"simple noise model. The expected output of a mirror circuit is always the "
"all-zeros bitstring, so the probability of measuring $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes "
"n}$ demonstrates how well each transpilation strategy preserves fidelity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengevaluasi dampak transpilasi pada fidelitas Circuit, buat mirror "
"circuits dari kasus 10-qubit dan jalankan di simulator Aer dengan noise "
"model sederhana. Output yang diharapkan dari mirror circuit selalu bitstring"
" all-zeros, sehingga probabilitas mengukur $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes n}$ "
"menunjukkan seberapa baik setiap strategi transpilasi mempertahankan "
"fidelitas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We ran both mirror circuits through the Aer simulator with a simple "
"depolarizing noise model. The survival probability, defined as the fraction "
"of shots that return the all-zeros bitstring, quantifies how much noise each"
" transpilation strategy introduces.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita menjalankan kedua mirror circuits melalui simulator Aer dengan noise "
"model depolarizing sederhana. Probabilitas bertahan hidup, yang "
"didefinisikan sebagai fraksi shot yang mengembalikan bitstring all-zeros, "
"mengkuantifikasi berapa banyak noise yang diperkenalkan oleh setiap strategi"
" transpilasi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format "
"{#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr ""
"Langkah 4: Post-process dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang "
"diinginkan {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-"
"format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We extract the probability of measuring the all-zeros bitstring from both "
"runs. A higher survival probability indicates better fidelity, meaning the "
"transpilation introduced less noise. The plot below shows the complement, 1 "
"- P(|0...0>), so that a lower bar indicates better fidelity and small "
"differences in error are easier to see.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mengekstrak probabilitas mengukur bitstring all-zeros dari kedua run. "
"Probabilitas bertahan hidup yang lebih tinggi menunjukkan fidelitas yang "
"lebih baik, artinya transpilasi memperkenalkan lebih sedikit noise. Plot di "
"bawah ini menunjukkan komplemen, 1 - P(|0...0>), sehingga bar yang lebih "
"rendah menunjukkan fidelitas yang lebih baik dan perbedaan kecil dalam error"
" lebih mudah dilihat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
"introduction/extracted-outputs/sim-step4-code-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output dari sel kode sebelumnya](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
"introduction/extracted-outputs/sim-step4-code-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case, the default transpiler produced both a shallower and smaller "
"circuit for this particular 10-qubit instance, so its higher fidelity is "
"expected. Per-circuit results vary: as the summary table above shows, the "
"AI-powered transpiler's advantage is in lower two-qubit depth on average, "
"not on every individual circuit. Which strategy yields higher fidelity "
"depends on the magnitude of the difference in each metric, the noise "
"characteristics of the hardware, and the structure of the circuit. Under a "
"uniform depolarizing noise model, total gate count often has a more direct "
"impact on accumulated error than depth alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kasus ini, transpiler default menghasilkan Circuit yang lebih dangkal "
"sekaligus lebih kecil untuk instance 10-qubit tertentu ini, sehingga "
"fidelitasnya yang lebih tinggi sudah diperkirakan. Hasil per-Circuit "
"bervariasi: seperti yang ditunjukkan tabel ringkasan di atas, keunggulan "
"Transpiler bertenaga AI adalah pada two-qubit depth yang lebih rendah rata-"
"rata, bukan pada setiap Circuit individual. Strategi mana yang menghasilkan "
"fidelitas lebih tinggi bergantung pada besarnya perbedaan setiap metrik, "
"karakteristik noise hardware, dan struktur Circuit. Di bawah noise model "
"depolarizing seragam, total jumlah Gate sering kali memiliki dampak yang "
"lebih langsung pada accumulated error daripada depth saja.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Contoh hardware skala besar {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Steps 1-4 {#steps-1-4}"
msgstr "Langkah 1-4 {#steps-1-4}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here all of these details are put together into a clear workflow at a larger"
" scale, which is then run on real quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini semua detail ini digabungkan menjadi alur kerja yang jelas pada "
"skala yang lebih besar, yang kemudian dijalankan pada hardware kuantum "
"nyata.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code below generates 25 random circuits with depth 8, where the number "
"of qubits ranges from 26 to 50. These circuits are then transpiled with both"
" strategies and the same metrics are collected. Then we build mirror "
"circuits from the 26-qubit case and submit them to the real backend.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kode di bawah ini membuat 25 Circuit acak dengan kedalaman 8, di mana jumlah"
" qubit berkisar dari 26 hingga 50. Circuit-Circuit ini kemudian "
"ditranspilasi dengan kedua strategi dan metrik yang sama dikumpulkan. "
"Kemudian kita membuat mirror circuits dari kasus 26-qubit dan mengirimkannya"
" ke Backend nyata.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
"introduction/extracted-outputs/hw-step2-plot-0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output dari sel kode sebelumnya](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
"introduction/extracted-outputs/hw-step2-plot-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/ai-transpiler-"
